      "text": "To solve this problem, we'll calculate the total number of possible outcomes and then subtract the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number.\n\n1. Calculate the total number of possible outcomes when rolling four dice:\n   - Each die has 6 possible outcomes.\n   - Thus, the total number of outcomes is given by \\(6^4\\).\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total number of outcomes} = 6^4\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number:\n   - There are 6 possible numbers (1 through 6) the dice could show.\n   - Thus, there are 6 possible outcomes where all four dice show the same number (one for each possible number).\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of outcomes where all dice show the same number} = 6\n   \\]\n\n3. Subtract the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number from the total number of outcomes to find the number of outcomes where not all four dice show the same number:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of outcomes where not all dice show the same number} = 6^4 - 6\n   \\]\n\n4. Count the number of 4-digit palindromes generated by the digits 3, 5, 6, 1 and 4 that creates a palindrome.\n   - The general form of a 4-digit palindrome is \\(\\overline{abba}\\).\n   - \\(a\\) can be 1 or 4 (since it can’t be 0).\n   - \\(b\\) can be 3, 5, or 6 (since it must be non-zero and different from \\(a\\)).\n   - Thus, for each choice of \\(a\\), there are 3 choices for \\(b\\).\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of 4-digit palindromes} = 2 \\times 3\n   \\]\n\n5. The probability that not all four dice show the same number, given that all six sides originally on the die are usable, is then:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Number of outcomes where not all dice show the same number}}{\\text{Total number of outcomes}} \n   \\]\n\nPutting it all together:\n\n\\[\n6^4 - 6 = 1296 - 6 = 1290\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Number of 4-digit palindromes} = 2 \\times 3 = 6\n\\]\n\nHence,\n\n\\[\n\\text{Probability} = \\frac{1290}{1290} = 1\n\\]\n\nHence the answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{1}\\)",
